## 3. Bootloader & Packaging Architecture Report

### Recommended Architecture: Staging Promotion Pipeline

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Build Lock Acquired] --> B[Phase 1: Clean build/]
    B --> C["Phase 2: PyInstaller via batmanoverlay.spec -> build/stage/"]
    C --> D[Phase 3: Package Portable Data Folders in Staging]
    D --> E[Phase 4: Full Boot Verification on Staging Binary]
    E --> F[Phase 5: Promote build/stage/ -> dist/batmanoverlay/]
    F --> G[Release Lock & Print Report]
```

### Why Staging Promotion Prevents Handle Locking
PyInstaller's `COLLECT` phase builds into `build/stage/batmanoverlay/`. Because `build/stage/` is an internal build folder, no external process (Explorer, indexers) ever holds a handle on it. PyInstaller's `shutil.rmtree` succeeds 100% of the time. Once verification succeeds, `scripts/build.py` promotes the files into `dist/batmanoverlay/` using non-destructive file copies.

